0..75 Comment "/// `leftOf` and `mkApplied` force a witness whose type decodes a call that"
76..104 Comment "/// returns a function type."
105..108 Comment "///"
109..189 Comment "/// Under the arm `B`, the type `holds(B)` of the witness is a call that returns"
190..243 Comment "/// a function type, so `leftOf` applies the witness."
244..321 Comment "/// The call `mk(B)` has the type `holds(B)` too, and `mkApplied` applies its"
322..346 Comment "/// result the same way."
347..410 Comment "/// The kernel admits each declaration as the checker does, and"
411..433 Comment "/// each fixture runs."
434..437 Comment "///"
438..516 Comment "/// The checker unfolds the type of the witness to the function type before it"
517..541 Comment "/// applies the witness."
542..622 Comment "/// The kernel reads the decode of the returned call by its own evaluator before"
623..666 Comment "/// it reads the shape of the forced value."
667..670 Comment "///"
671..687 Comment "/// - see: #6057"
688..721 Comment "/// - see: `refined-binder.gandr`"
